    "result": "Perfect! All requirements have been successfully implemented and verified. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` to allow CI pipelines to gate on metric scores.\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **frai-core/src/eval/index.js**\n   - Added threshold validation and parsing logic\n   - Modified `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n   - Reports now include `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields when thresholds are provided\n   - Metrics without scores (null) automatically fail their thresholds\n\n2. **frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js**\n   - Updated Markdown reports to include a \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n\n3. **frai-cli/src/index.ts**\n   - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable)\n   - Parses thresholds and validates format, values (0-1 range), and metric IDs\n   - Exit codes: 0 if all pass, 1 if any fail, 2 if malformed/invalid\n   - Error messages list valid metric IDs when unknown metric is specified\n\n4. **README.md**\n   - Documented the new `--threshold` option with valid metrics and usage examples\n\n### All Task Requirements Verified \u2705\n\n- Build succeeds: `pnpm --filter frai run build` exits 0\n- No new test failures: `pnpm --filter frai-core test` has only the 2 pre-existing failures\n- Backward compatible: Reports without thresholds have same keys as before\n- Two passing thresholds: Exit 0, report has `passed: true` with threshold entries\n- Failing threshold: Exit 1, report has `passed: false`\n- No-score metrics: Fail their thresholds (e.g., exact_match without references)\n- Markdown format: \"Thresholds\" section shows PASS/FAIL for each\n- Error handling: Malformed threshold/invalid range/unknown metric exit 2 with descriptive messages\n- SDK support: `generateReport()` accepts `thresholds` parameter and works with custom metrics\n- Documentation: `--threshold` option documented in README",
